        "original_id": "646f92ba-6dc3-5222-b275-f7019d62b188",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: French Bulldog, American Bulldog\n- Places: England, Paris, France\n- Concepts: dog breeds, breed types, breed origins\n\nFacts:\n- In the 1800s, French Bulldog originated from a cross between bulldog ancestors imported from England and local ratters in Paris, France.\n- French Bulldog is also known as the Frenchie.\n- French Bulldog is a small breed of domestic dog.\n- American Bulldog is a breed of utility dog.\n- American Bulldog has two specific types called Standard and Classic.\n- American Bulldog also includes mixes of the Standard and Classic types.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "6ea56c7e-f524-54db-9d2d-16c9f4dc713c",
        "text": "Page: French Bulldog. Sentence: The French Bulldog also known as the Frenchie is a small breed of domestic dog.\nPage: French Bulldog. Sentence: Frenchies were the result in the 1800s of a cross between bulldog ancestors imported from England and local ratters in Paris (France).\nPage: American Bulldog. Sentence: The American Bulldog is a breed of utility dog.\nPage: American Bulldog. Sentence: There are two specific types of American Bulldog, Standard and Classic; additionally, there are also mixes of the two types.",
